01:18:10.920 --> 01:18:11.753
Steve?
- Well, there was

01:18:11.753 --> 01:18:12.586
a comment on QOF,

01:18:12.586 --> 01:18:15.044
which some of you might
have heard me make before.

01:18:15.044 --> 01:18:16.981
I think it's important,

01:18:16.981 --> 01:18:18.150
although it is in the section here

01:18:18.150 --> 01:18:20.580
on cutting bureaucracy
that we don't confuse it,

01:18:20.580 --> 01:18:22.710
that it's a bureaucratic process

01:18:22.710 --> 01:18:25.740
because it's actually an
incentivization process

01:18:25.740 --> 01:18:27.570
to promote a set of interventions

01:18:27.570 --> 01:18:29.853
that we know improve patient outcomes.

01:18:29.853 --> 01:18:30.720
- Yes.
- For instance,

01:18:30.720 --> 01:18:34.920
in identifying poor blood
pressure control or hypertension,

01:18:34.920 --> 01:18:36.900
managing blood pressure control,

01:18:36.900 --> 01:18:40.410
lipid management, managing diabetes.

01:18:40.410 --> 01:18:42.330
And there is published
evidence for instance,

01:18:42.330 --> 01:18:45.210
in evidence that for instance
in diabetes that it leads

01:18:45.210 --> 01:18:48.750
to an improvement of real
improvements in patient outcomes.

01:18:48.750 --> 01:18:52.380
So, the point here is to
ensure that it is doing

01:18:52.380 --> 01:18:54.120
what it's intended to do,

01:18:54.120 --> 01:18:56.820
which is to drive improvements

01:18:56.820 --> 01:18:59.730
and to try and streamline processes,

01:18:59.730 --> 01:19:04.730
so that in a sense the more
bureaucratic element of it

01:19:05.040 --> 01:19:07.230
is removed, but at the same time

01:19:07.230 --> 01:19:10.003
those incentivization
- Migrations.

01:19:10.003 --> 01:19:11.880
- to improve outcomes remain.

01:19:11.880 --> 01:19:14.130
So that is a task for this year,

01:19:14.130 --> 01:19:16.650
but it's important to
remember it does drive

01:19:16.650 --> 01:19:18.540
good clinical outcomes.

01:19:18.540 --> 01:19:21.780
- Thank you, very good. So Laura?

01:19:21.780 --> 01:19:23.340
- One's really a comment actually,

01:19:23.340 --> 01:19:26.520
which was to note 'cause you've said

01:19:26.520 --> 01:19:30.013
I've been on the Board
since 2018, I think it is.

01:19:32.553 --> 01:19:36.300
What you published last week
is a really good example

01:19:36.300 --> 01:19:40.680
of where we have managed to put technology

01:19:40.680 --> 01:19:42.930
at the heart of what we are doing.

01:19:42.930 --> 01:19:45.960
And I think that is enormous,

01:19:45.960 --> 01:19:47.550
that is enormously different.

01:19:47.550 --> 01:19:49.560
I can't kind of stress
just how different it is

01:19:49.560 --> 01:19:53.250
in the sense of the idea
that 90% of patients

01:19:53.250 --> 01:19:56.460
will be able to use the app to interact.

01:19:56.460 --> 01:19:59.190
That then frees up time for
people who choose not to.

01:19:59.190 --> 01:20:00.600
But it's the fact that we've embedded it

01:20:00.600 --> 01:20:02.430
in the whole thought process

01:20:02.430 --> 01:20:04.680
of how we address the issue

01:20:04.680 --> 01:20:06.420
that I really just wanted to call out

01:20:06.420 --> 01:20:09.180
and say how exciting I think it is,

01:20:09.180 --> 01:20:11.280
and hopefully demonstrating

01:20:11.280 --> 01:20:14.160
kind of why it's worth persisting

01:20:14.160 --> 01:20:16.890
with some of the kind
of core basic investment

01:20:16.890 --> 01:20:18.330
that makes that possible.

01:20:18.330 --> 01:20:20.610
So it's kind of, that stuff only works

01:20:20.610 --> 01:20:22.170
when you can actually join up stuff

01:20:22.170 --> 01:20:24.595
in the back, so thank you.

01:20:24.595 --> 01:20:25.770
- It's the last, so I'll
get Andrew to come in.

01:20:25.770 --> 01:20:26.910
And you might want to just reflect back

01:20:26.910 --> 01:20:28.830
