are giving enough flexibility

01:20:44.790 --> 01:20:47.550
to general practise to
move the various packages

01:20:47.550 --> 01:20:50.910
of allocation and money that they get

01:20:50.910 --> 01:20:53.820
in order to, you know, benefit patients.

01:20:53.820 --> 01:20:58.680
And some practises I know say
this inhibits their ability

01:20:58.680 --> 01:21:00.750
to be flexible and to meet the needs

01:21:00.750 --> 01:21:03.870
of their particular group of patients.

01:21:03.870 --> 01:21:06.150
So, it's not in the plan,

01:21:06.150 --> 01:21:08.070
but it's just a thought really
around is there anything

01:21:08.070 --> 01:21:12.090
we can do at NHS England level or DH level

01:21:12.090 --> 01:21:13.650
that would help there.

01:21:13.650 --> 01:21:15.810
- And it came up actually
at the round table

01:21:15.810 --> 01:21:18.628
yesterday morning actually where you were.

01:21:18.628 --> 01:21:20.190
- Mm-hmm.
- Do you want to react

01:21:20.190 --> 01:21:22.290
to those questions and comments?

01:21:22.290 --> 01:21:26.253
- Yeah, so pharmacy, first of all,

01:21:27.210 --> 01:21:31.290
all the pharmacists and
the pharmacy organisations

01:21:31.290 --> 01:21:33.930
I've spoken to, which is quite a lot

01:21:33.930 --> 01:21:37.323
over the past couple of weeks
are really excited by this.

01:21:38.580 --> 01:21:40.920
We are still in,

01:21:40.920 --> 01:21:42.510
well, we started negotiations

01:21:42.510 --> 01:21:45.510
with the Pharmaceutical
Services Negotiating Committee,

01:21:45.510 --> 01:21:49.080
as to how we write into the
contract the pharmacy first,

01:21:49.080 --> 01:21:51.060
which we are obliged to do,

01:21:51.060 --> 01:21:53.700
but they have welcomed it
