01:21:53.700 --> 01:21:55.830
and I think it's worth saying

01:21:55.830 --> 01:21:58.080
it's because they see it for what it is,

01:21:58.080 --> 01:22:02.250
as the first step in a
strategy for community pharmacy

01:22:02.250 --> 01:22:06.270
to be a key part of that
integrated offer to patients

01:22:06.270 --> 01:22:07.950
for clinical services.

01:22:07.950 --> 01:22:10.920
So not a largely dispensing service

01:22:10.920 --> 01:22:14.070
with a bit of clinical
services tacked on the side,

01:22:14.070 --> 01:22:16.530
but moving over time in the direction

01:22:16.530 --> 01:22:19.320
of a clinical service deliverer,

01:22:19.320 --> 01:22:21.510
- Yeah.
- with dispensing

01:22:21.510 --> 01:22:24.060
as a key part of the business alongside,

01:22:24.060 --> 01:22:25.980
and that's really exciting.

01:22:25.980 --> 01:22:28.230
From 2026, all graduate pharmacists

01:22:28.230 --> 01:22:30.060
will be independent prescribers

01:22:30.060 --> 01:22:32.310
and that gives us another real opportunity

01:22:32.310 --> 01:22:33.843
for a step change.

01:22:34.680 --> 01:22:37.350
I thought you were going to ask me

01:22:37.350 --> 01:22:39.542
