01:22:41.220 --> 01:22:44.520
but part of this package

01:22:44.520 --> 01:22:47.670
is an NIHR study

01:22:47.670 --> 01:22:50.580
evaluating how we implement this to ensure

01:22:50.580 --> 01:22:52.599
that we are not increasing the risk,

01:22:52.599 --> 01:22:54.210
- Yeah.
- but these PGDs

01:22:54.210 --> 01:22:56.040
are established, and they're the ones

01:22:56.040 --> 01:22:59.250
that nurse practitioners or
nurses in general practise

01:22:59.250 --> 01:23:03.330
might follow quite safely
under supervision of GPs.

01:23:03.330 --> 01:23:07.290
And so we are not concerned,
but we want to make sure,

01:23:07.290 --> 01:23:09.000
but yeah, really positive,

01:23:09.000 --> 01:23:10.550
- Thank you.
- quite exciting.

01:23:12.300 --> 01:23:14.040
Steve's absolutely right about QOF.

01:23:14.040 --> 01:23:18.270
Just to comment, we have
committed to review QOF this year,

01:23:18.270 --> 01:23:20.310
partly because we want to make sure

01:23:20.310 --> 01:23:22.440
we continue to focus on

01:23:22.440 --> 01:23:27.270
the most important clinical
priorities for incentivization.

01:23:27.270 --> 01:23:31.890
And I certainly, and not many clinicians

01:23:31.890 --> 01:23:34.927
in this organisation or
more widely are saying,

01:23:34.927 --> 01:23:36.180
"Abolish it completely."

01:23:36.180 --> 01:23:38.160
What people are saying is, "Let's look."

01:23:38.160 --> 01:23:39.600
- Yeah.
- Is it the most appropriate?

01:23:39.600 --> 01:23:40.890
And is it the best way

01:23:40.890 --> 01:23:43.170
to deliver clinical improvement?

01:23:43.170 --> 01:23:47.190
So what role does transparent benchmarked,

01:23:47.190 --> 01:23:49.200
clinical outcome data hold

01:23:49.200 --> 01:23:52.800
versus financial
incentivization of processes?

01:23:52.800 --> 01:23:56.490
We started to talk to the
national clinical directors

01:23:56.490 --> 01:23:58.080
who are very supportive of going through

01:23:58.080 --> 01:23:59.340
this process with us.

01:23:59.340 --> 01:24:02.140
So, we're taking very great care

01:24:03.298 --> 01:24:04.623
that we get this right.

01:24:06.450 --> 01:24:08.391
Thank you, Laura.

01:24:08.391 --> 01:24:09.810
Yes.

01:24:09.810 --> 01:24:12.183
I'm very excited to.
- Noted, noted, yeah.

01:24:13.020 --> 01:24:16.020
- And funding flexibility,

01:24:16.020 --> 01:24:19.410
one of the reasons that we
have made the change we made

01:24:19.410 --> 01:24:21.360
for the Investment Impact Fund

01:24:21.360 --> 01:24:24.450
is that very much don't
just use that funding

01:24:24.450 --> 01:24:27.780
to do those processes that
were in those 31 targets

01:24:27.780 --> 01:24:31.260
that we've moved aside this year.

01:24:31.260 --> 01:24:34.650
Use it flexibly to deliver
what your community most needs,

01:24:34.650 --> 01:24:35.790
as far as access goes,

01:24:35.790 --> 01:24:38.010
and have the money in your budgets,

01:24:38.010 --> 01:24:39.860
so that you can employ staff with it.

01:24:41.160 --> 01:24:43.350
But with things like the
additional roles money,

01:24:43.350 --> 01:24:46.770
we've widened the number
of roles this year

01:24:46.770 --> 01:24:49.863
so practises have more choice
of what they will most need.

01:24:51.540 --> 01:24:54.060
But alongside the QOF review

01:24:54.060 --> 01:24:56.670
and some of the other
reviews for next year,

01:24:56.670 --> 01:24:58.170
some of the questions we're asking,

01:24:58.170 --> 01:25:01.530
the big questions are to what extent is it

01:25:01.530 --> 01:25:04.440
a one-size-fits-all national approach,

01:25:04.440 --> 01:25:06.480
or do we need to work with ICBs

01:25:06.480 --> 01:25:09.120
over what local flexibility
around some of this.

01:25:09.120 --> 01:25:12.180
So, there's a big chunk of work,

01:25:12.180 --> 01:25:15.480
quite strategic work in how
we approach the contract

01:25:15.480 --> 01:25:16.313
- Thank you.
- when the end

01:25:16.313 --> 01:25:17.610
of the five year contract period

01:25:17.610 --> 01:25:19.399
comes at the end of this year.
- Thank you.

01:25:19.399 --> 01:25:20.602
I know it's a very dangerous thing,

01:25:20.602 --> 01:25:21.632
but I know the Finance Director

01:25:21.632 --> 01:25:22.468
wants to make a comment,

01:25:22.468 --> 01:25:23.748
I think, so.
- Yeah.

01:25:23.748 --> 01:25:25.350
My comment was going to be,

01:25:25.350 --> 01:25:27.570
I mean actually it's quite a big change

01:25:27.570 --> 01:25:29.790
in some of the kind of incentive
structure we put in place.

01:25:29.790 --> 01:25:32.130
Now, there is a bit of a test in it too

