01:55:28.290 --> 01:55:31.260
for the NHS, actually more than 60% of it,

01:55:31.260 --> 01:55:33.750
is spent in the field.

01:55:33.750 --> 01:55:34.583
It is not-
- In the systems, yeah.

01:55:34.583 --> 01:55:36.019
- It is not us,
- Yeah.

01:55:36.019 --> 01:55:37.470
Central, yeah.
- purchasing things,

01:55:37.470 --> 01:55:40.470
they are purchasing things for themselves,

01:55:40.470 --> 01:55:44.400
but we are more and more working
collaboratively with them

01:55:44.400 --> 01:55:47.520
to make decisions about our priorities.

01:55:47.520 --> 01:55:50.910
You also made a very good
point, Amanda, about commercial.

01:55:50.910 --> 01:55:52.200
Now how we...

01:55:52.200 --> 01:55:53.430
I have been,

01:55:53.430 --> 01:55:55.860
I have learned so much from Jacqui Rock

01:55:55.860 --> 01:55:58.290
about our commercial efforts,

01:55:58.290 --> 01:56:02.820
and we are moving into a new territory

01:56:02.820 --> 01:56:06.870
around our approach to the
adoption of innovation,

01:56:06.870 --> 01:56:10.980
and how we approach the
commercial aspects of this.

01:56:10.980 --> 01:56:13.605
And I just want to make a distinction

01:56:13.605 --> 01:56:16.200
between true innovation,

01:56:16.200 --> 01:56:18.720
where it is a singular supplier,

01:56:18.720 --> 01:56:20.520
it's a first in kind,

01:56:20.520 --> 01:56:23.130
and we approach that one way,

01:56:23.130 --> 01:56:26.250
but when things become commodities,

01:56:26.250 --> 01:56:30.750
as they move from singular and brand new

01:56:30.750 --> 01:56:32.700
all the way to a commodity,

01:56:32.700 --> 01:56:35.400
we should be moving
our commercial approach

01:56:35.400 --> 01:56:37.410
along that same continuum.

01:56:37.410 --> 01:56:39.210
And when it's a commodity,

01:56:39.210 --> 01:56:41.580
we should more and more be purchasing,

01:56:41.580 --> 01:56:45.540
using that national
throw weight of the NHS

01:56:45.540 --> 01:56:47.430
to get the best possible deal,

01:56:47.430 --> 01:56:50.460
as we have for quite a
while with pharmaceuticals.

01:56:50.460 --> 01:56:52.230
- Yes.
- We should be doing that

01:56:52.230 --> 01:56:54.630
with technology, but only in the subset

01:56:54.630 --> 01:56:57.914
where it is appropriate that-
- Okay.

01:56:57.914 --> 01:56:59.722
I'm going to speed you up in your answers.

01:56:59.722 --> 01:57:01.560
- Okay, okay, okay.
- I've got two more.

01:57:01.560 --> 01:57:04.500
- So, they're very important
about the disenfranchisement

01:57:04.500 --> 01:57:07.830
and digital exclusion, so it's
a very important question.

01:57:07.830 --> 01:57:11.040
I will echo at least part
of what Richard said,

01:57:11.040 --> 01:57:15.300
which is it does actually free up space.

01:57:15.300 --> 01:57:19.440
So, if the phone is
available to be answered,

01:57:19.440 --> 01:57:24.420
if 30, 40, 50% of people are
booking their own appointment,

01:57:24.420 --> 01:57:26.400
right, and so suddenly that person

01:57:26.400 --> 01:57:28.650
who didn't have time to answer your call,

01:57:28.650 --> 01:57:29.820
one of the things that was interesting

01:57:29.820 --> 01:57:34.820
when we automated this mass general was,

01:57:34.830 --> 01:57:36.450
when we automated appointments,

01:57:36.450 --> 01:57:40.770
was actually our patient
satisfaction scores

01:57:40.770 --> 01:57:45.770
for in-office receptivity went way up.

01:57:47.010 --> 01:57:51.720
And that was because the
people sitting at the desk

01:57:51.720 --> 01:57:54.990
greeting patients were
actually greeting patients,

01:57:54.990 --> 01:57:57.060
rather than on the phone
- Yeah.

01:57:57.060 --> 01:57:59.040
- asking people to wait.

01:57:59.040 --> 01:58:01.170
You know, it's sort of an interesting,

01:58:01.170 --> 01:58:03.030
important piece of this.

01:58:03.030 --> 01:58:07.950
The other one is a great
thing about digitising process

01:58:07.950 --> 01:58:10.650
is that you suddenly have data

01:58:10.650 --> 01:58:12.360
on who is using that process,

01:58:12.360 --> 01:58:14.850
and who was being left
out of that process.

01:58:14.850 --> 01:58:17.850
And I just want to point out
that's exactly what happened

01:58:17.850 --> 01:58:20.520
with the vaccine programme with Covid.

01:58:20.520 --> 01:58:25.080
We had data on who the
vaccine programme was missing

01:58:25.080 --> 01:58:28.080
that allows you to target groups

01:58:28.080 --> 01:58:30.870
to make sure that groups
aren't disenfranchised.

01:58:30.870 --> 01:58:32.010
- Yeah.
- So that data is

01:58:32.010 --> 01:58:36.900
a critical piece of what
you get, so it requires

01:58:36.900 --> 01:58:38.340
vigilance to make sure
- Okay.

01:58:38.340 --> 01:58:39.210
- that you're not disenfranchised.

01:58:39.210 --> 01:58:40.105
- [Richard] Thank you, Tim.

01:58:40.105 --> 01:58:40.938
I am going to stop you here
- Okay.

01:58:40.938 --> 01:58:43.770
- to give Laura, you want
to make the closing remarks

01:58:43.770 --> 01:58:45.080
on this item because I want to go

01:58:45.080 --> 01:58:46.567
to the National Guardians update actually,

01:58:46.567 --> 01:58:47.940
and we've still got

01:58:47.940 --> 01:58:49.350
Specific Equality Duties.
_ I will be brief.

01:58:49.350 --> 01:58:52.320
It was really just to
leave the Board I guess

01:58:52.320 --> 01:58:55.770
with a the kind of thought
about what its responsibility

01:58:55.770 --> 01:58:57.540
might be in this space
and the opportunity.

01:58:57.540 --> 01:58:59.400
'Cause I think it is hugely exciting.

01:58:59.400 --> 01:59:03.330
I think the first is that
that core infrastructure,

01:59:03.330 --> 01:59:06.330
so whether it's the Spine, et cetera,

01:59:06.330 --> 01:59:09.660
that enables all of
this isn't an accident,

01:59:09.660 --> 01:59:11.100
and actually you are
- Okay.

01:59:11.100 --> 01:59:12.100
- the guardians of it.

01:59:12.100 --> 01:59:13.709
- Yeah.
- It needs money.

01:59:13.709 --> 01:59:15.060
- Needs to be invested.
- It needs investment.

01:59:15.060 --> 01:59:18.090
It needs because otherwise none
of the other magic happens,

01:59:18.090 --> 01:59:20.640
and you are the guardians
of a large chunk of that.

01:59:21.667 --> 01:59:25.410
I think the second is that
where we've got this right,

01:59:25.410 --> 01:59:27.810
actually we do something that we find hard

01:59:27.810 --> 01:59:28.950
in the Health Services,

01:59:28.950 --> 01:59:31.320
we take, we put the patient

01:59:31.320 --> 01:59:33.000
and the fact that they're trying to deal

01:59:33.000 --> 01:59:35.460
with their pathway first,

01:59:35.460 --> 01:59:38.220
rather than we think
about the care setting,

01:59:38.220 --> 01:59:39.053
and we actually kind of

01:59:39.053 --> 01:59:40.170
join it up like that.
- Yeah.

01:59:40.170 --> 01:59:41.943
- And then I think the third is,

01:59:44.170 --> 01:59:45.870
a lot of the pathway transformation

01:59:45.870 --> 01:59:49.380
does very dramatic
things to our workforce,

01:59:49.380 --> 01:59:51.000
and to the skills we need.

01:59:51.000 --> 01:59:54.210
And I think that engagement
and thinking that through

01:59:54.210 --> 01:59:56.220
- Mm-hmm.
- is hugely important.

01:59:56.220 --> 01:59:57.630
Whether it's in the workforce plan,

01:59:57.630 --> 01:59:59.220
whether it's working
with the royal colleges

01:59:59.220 --> 02:00:02.790
about how do we think differently
about roles in the future.

02:00:02.790 --> 02:00:05.160
But I think that's another
really important area

02:00:05.160 --> 02:00:05.993
for you, the Board.

02:00:05.993 --> 02:00:08.100
So I would say those three things,

02:00:08.100 --> 02:00:09.750
the infrastructure isn't an accident,

02:00:09.750 --> 02:00:11.340
you are the guardians of it.

02:00:11.340 --> 02:00:13.980
The patient focus is where the,

02:00:13.980 --> 02:00:15.270
kind of, how the magic happens.

02:00:15.270 --> 02:00:17.430
And the third is really pay attention

02:00:17.430 --> 02:00:20.070
to the workforce consequences of this,

02:00:20.070 --> 02:00:22.017
and how we take people with us.

02:00:22.017 --> 02:00:22.850
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

02:00:22.850 --> 02:00:24.780
- Right, I am going to move us on.

02:00:24.780 --> 02:00:27.993
Jane, you have joined us
as our National Guardian.

02:00:29.100 --> 02:00:31.350
You've given us a paper.

02:00:31.350 --> 02:00:32.430
We have a paper,

02:00:32.430 --> 02:00:37.430
thank you very much, on an
update actually on speaking up.

02:00:37.680 --> 02:00:40.680
And can I just hand to
you for the key points

02:00:40.680 --> 02:00:42.300
you want to make sure
that we've registered

02:00:42.300 --> 02:00:44.310
from the update paper?

02:00:44.310 --> 02:00:45.330
- Thank you very much, Chair,

02:00:45.330 --> 02:00:47.130
and thank you ladies and
gentlemen, good afternoon.

02:00:47.130 --> 02:00:48.300
It's really great to join you.

02:00:48.300 --> 02:00:49.767
I can't believe it's been a
year since I was last with you.

02:00:49.767 --> 02:00:51.963
I don't know where that year's gone,

02:00:53.130 --> 02:00:55.650
but just really important to
focus on a couple of elements,

02:00:55.650 --> 02:00:56.880
and I will take it as read,

02:00:56.880 --> 02:00:58.500
that you've read your papers,

02:00:58.500 --> 02:01:01.440
and I'd be happy to take
questions or comments

02:01:01.440 --> 02:01:04.830
on anything in the update or
indeed in the annual report,

02:01:04.830 --> 02:01:06.090
which there is a link to.

02:01:06.090 --> 02:01:08.100
It was late being laid before Parliament

02:01:08.100 --> 02:01:10.830
because of the government
changes, no fault of our own.

02:01:10.830 --> 02:01:13.680
It was there and then the
Prime Minister resigned,

02:01:13.680 --> 02:01:16.710
and it waited a very long
time to get a slot back on.

02:01:16.710 --> 02:01:18.390
But there's some important
findings in there

02:01:18.390 --> 02:01:20.700
that I want to pull out,
not just from there,

02:01:20.700 --> 02:01:23.490
but also what's been
happening more recently.

02:01:23.490 --> 02:01:26.670
And just to remind us that
in the NHS People Plan

02:01:26.670 --> 02:01:27.750
there is the people promise

02:01:27.750 --> 02:01:30.780
of every worker will
have a voice that counts.

02:01:30.780 --> 02:01:33.030
And that is partly what
my office and I exist

02:01:33.030 --> 02:01:35.640
to help support
organisations in looking at,

02:01:35.640 --> 02:01:37.200
not just obviously through

02:01:37.200 --> 02:01:38.640
the Freedom to Speak Up Guardian route,

02:01:38.640 --> 02:01:41.970
'cause that is just a
one very small route,

02:01:41.970 --> 02:01:43.440
a very important safety route,

02:01:43.440 --> 02:01:45.690
if you can't speak to
your line manager, to HR,

02:01:45.690 --> 02:01:48.360
to patient safety, to your leadership.

02:01:48.360 --> 02:01:53.360
And it's as important for
all the NHS organisations

02:01:53.460 --> 02:01:55.920
that exist as well as the national bodies.

02:01:55.920 --> 02:01:59.820
And we now have over a 1,000 guardians

02:01:59.820 --> 02:02:03.210
across a number of organisational types,

02:02:03.210 --> 02:02:05.820
and that's increasingly growing.

02:02:05.820 --> 02:02:09.750
We also have interest
from other public bodies,

02:02:09.750 --> 02:02:13.717
police, fire and rescue,
government departments saying,

02:02:13.717 --> 02:02:15.180
"What are you doing in the NHS,

02:02:15.180 --> 02:02:17.070
and what difference is it making?"

02:02:17.070 --> 02:02:21.420
And I am confident that in many places

02:02:21.420 --> 02:02:23.730
it is making a difference in the sense

02:02:23.730 --> 02:02:25.800
of people are speaking to their guardians.

02:02:25.800 --> 02:02:29.100
Guardians are carrying out
that role of shining a light

02:02:29.100 --> 02:02:32.490
within organisations
around what improvements

02:02:32.490 --> 02:02:35.010
and what being that
ambassador's cultural change

02:02:35.010 --> 02:02:36.870
that Sir Robert Francis saw.

02:02:36.870 --> 02:02:38.967
However, and that's the big however,

02:02:38.967 --> 02:02:42.200
and I think the biggest
message I want to draw

02:02:42.200 --> 02:02:45.240
to your attention and maybe
to discuss with you today is,

02:02:45.240 --> 02:02:47.490
yet again this year in the staff survey,

02:02:47.490 --> 02:02:51.540
we have seen a decline in the
confidence of our workforce

02:02:51.540 --> 02:02:54.420
in their ability to both
speak up and feel confident

02:02:54.420 --> 02:02:57.060
that if they do speak up,
something will be done about it,

02:02:57.060 --> 02:02:58.770
and that's through all those roots.

02:02:58.770 --> 02:03:01.110
And that's really worrying. I
hoped last year it was a blip.

02:03:01.110 --> 02:03:04.140
It was a post-Covid blip,
but it's clearly not a blip.

02:03:04.140 --> 02:03:06.240
This is a second year of a decline,

02:03:06.240 --> 02:03:08.430
and it's more than a wake up call.

02:03:08.430 --> 02:03:11.760
And I wonder, obviously
myself and my office exist

02:03:11.760 --> 02:03:13.350
for three reasons, to train,

02:03:13.350 --> 02:03:15.600
lead, and develop the
network of guardians,

02:03:15.600 --> 02:03:19.050
to carry out the reviews
of where best practise

02:03:19.050 --> 02:03:20.400
isn't being implemented around,

02:03:20.400 --> 02:03:21.900
you know, speaking up,

02:03:21.900 --> 02:03:25.020
and thirdly, to be that
voice into the system

02:03:25.020 --> 02:03:27.660
of our speaking up culture across the NHS.

02:03:27.660 --> 02:03:29.557
And that voice today is saying,

02:03:29.557 --> 02:03:31.200
"We've got a problem."

02:03:31.200 --> 02:03:33.810
You know, we have
repeated high profile case

02:03:33.810 --> 02:03:35.730
after high profile case.

02:03:35.730 --> 02:03:37.230
When we see that workers,

02:03:37.230 --> 02:03:39.180
if they do have the courage to speak up,

02:03:39.180 --> 02:03:42.750
and believe that, you know,
their voice will count

02:03:42.750 --> 02:03:44.610
that they're suffering detriment for it.

02:03:44.610 --> 02:03:46.350
There's a statistic in here

02:03:46.350 --> 02:03:48.480
that with the data that we collect,

02:03:48.480 --> 02:03:53.480
and that's just from cases that
go to guardians, not wider,

02:03:53.790 --> 02:03:56.010
but we're seeing a steady increase

02:03:56.010 --> 02:03:58.230
in the number of guardians
who are reporting

02:03:58.230 --> 02:04:01.140
detriment happening to
workers who speak up,

02:04:01.140 --> 02:04:04.140
and obviously we see that
in the high profile cases.

02:04:04.140 --> 02:04:06.390
So my question to you as a Board,

02:04:06.390 --> 02:04:08.940
and next week I'm going to CQC

02:04:08.940 --> 02:04:11.550
to report to my other funding body,

02:04:11.550 --> 02:04:15.300
is what more, as regulators
and as leaders in the system,

02:04:15.300 --> 02:04:18.540
do we need to be doing in order to hold

02:04:18.540 --> 02:04:21.780
our leadership to account
to really focus in,

02:04:21.780 --> 02:04:23.730
yes, the performance, the delivery?

02:04:23.730 --> 02:04:26.490
You know, hearing today
of the improvements

02:04:26.490 --> 02:04:28.830
is absolutely vital.

02:04:28.830 --> 02:04:31.020
But without a workforce that can speak up

02:04:31.020 --> 02:04:34.230
particularly about patient
safety and worker safety issues,

02:04:34.230 --> 02:04:38.850
we're going to have more
patient harm, more worker harm,

02:04:38.850 --> 02:04:41.643
and ultimately the quality
of service won't be there.

02:04:43.650 --> 02:04:45.600
It's not all doom and
gloom, and I hope that,

02:04:45.600 --> 02:04:48.197
you know, but I think
that's my stark message

02:04:48.197 --> 02:04:49.527
that I want to give today,

02:04:49.527 --> 02:04:50.883
and I hope you see that.

02:04:51.780 --> 02:04:53.313
Obviously there's an update
in the paper on the work

02:04:53.313 --> 02:04:55.500
that we've been doing over the last year.

02:04:55.500 --> 02:04:57.720
I'm really delighted to
announce the strengthening

02:04:57.720 --> 02:05:00.216
of our governance of the
National Guardian's Office.

02:05:00.216 --> 02:05:03.270
Obviously under the
leadership of Sir Andrew

02:05:03.270 --> 02:05:05.640
and Sir Robert Francis,
before he retired last year

02:05:05.640 --> 02:05:07.290
of our Accountability and Liaison Board.

02:05:07.290 --> 02:05:09.810
Last year I reported, we were increasing

02:05:09.810 --> 02:05:11.940
the strength of the Board
by bringing on executives

02:05:11.940 --> 02:05:13.980
from the funding bodies and
from the Department of Health

02:05:13.980 --> 02:05:15.090
and Social Care.

02:05:15.090 --> 02:05:16.740
We now, as of this month,

02:05:16.740 --> 02:05:20.430
have appointed Suzanne McCarthy
as our independent chair

02:05:20.430 --> 02:05:23.550
to work with the non-execs
and executive on that Board

02:05:23.550 --> 02:05:26.610
to help give greater scrutiny
to what we do as an office,

02:05:26.610 --> 02:05:27.537
what I do as the National Guardian,

02:05:27.537 --> 02:05:30.207
and how we spend the
funding that you give us,

02:05:30.207 --> 02:05:33.120
and CQC give us for our accountability.

02:05:33.120 --> 02:05:35.430
And also to help be that voice

02:05:35.430 --> 02:05:38.490
to the wider partners

02:05:38.490 --> 02:05:39.930
around what we need to be doing

02:05:39.930 --> 02:05:41.437
to ensure that we don't have,

02:05:41.437 --> 02:05:43.530
you know, another mid Staffs,

02:05:43.530 --> 02:05:48.530
that we don't have another
"Ockenden Report" needed,

02:05:48.660 --> 02:05:49.717
another "Bill Kirkup Report".

02:05:49.717 --> 02:05:52.473
You know, they're listed
in here and they go on.

02:05:53.790 --> 02:05:57.330
So, obviously, the close working that I do

02:05:57.330 --> 02:05:59.790
with key stakeholders, as well
as with individual guardians,

02:05:59.790 --> 02:06:00.623
is really important.

02:06:00.623 --> 02:06:02.640
And I'd want to highlight
just a couple of things

02:06:02.640 --> 02:06:05.340
in a couple of moments
before closing comments.

02:06:05.340 --> 02:06:07.260
And that's to thank Ruth May

02:06:07.260 --> 02:06:09.000
and the work of Jennifer Caguioa

02:06:09.000 --> 02:06:10.290
around international nurses.

02:06:10.290 --> 02:06:13.620
I'm really aware through the
evidence base that we have

02:06:13.620 --> 02:06:17.820
of the disproportionate effect of people

02:06:17.820 --> 02:06:19.830
from Black and minority ethnic groups

02:06:19.830 --> 02:06:21.660
in their ability to speak up and be heard,

02:06:21.660 --> 02:06:24.240
and indeed suffer detriment
and retaliatory referrals

02:06:24.240 --> 02:06:25.560
to professional bodies.

02:06:25.560 --> 02:06:27.240
And it's really important that work

02:06:27.240 --> 02:06:28.320
with international recruits,

02:06:28.320 --> 02:06:32.610
and we're doing some
jointly with Ruth and Jeni,

02:06:32.610 --> 02:06:36.150
and also with the Nursing
and Midwifery Council.

02:06:36.150 --> 02:06:37.290
Any learning that we take

02:06:37.290 --> 02:06:41.040
from the international
nursing midwifery workforce,

02:06:41.040 --> 02:06:43.350
obviously we want to take out
to all international recruits.

02:06:43.350 --> 02:06:45.570
You know, it's just as important
that international recruits

02:06:45.570 --> 02:06:48.630
who are doctors, or who
are in our housekeeping

02:06:48.630 --> 02:06:49.890
and domestic services

02:06:49.890 --> 02:06:53.100
all understand the expectations
of the culture here,

02:06:53.100 --> 02:06:55.380
which can be very different
from other countries,

02:06:55.380 --> 02:06:57.630
so an important piece of work.

02:06:57.630 --> 02:06:59.610
And also this year I've
really welcomed opportunities

02:06:59.610 --> 02:07:03.150
to contribute to some major
reviews like the Hewitt Review,

02:07:03.150 --> 02:07:08.100
the "Being Fair Report"
that NHS Resolution

02:07:08.100 --> 02:07:09.660
have just recently published,

02:07:09.660 --> 02:07:12.420
and also the Kark
Implementation Working Group.

02:07:12.420 --> 02:07:15.300
All really important areas of work,

02:07:15.300 --> 02:07:18.990
the freedom to speak up and
improving psychological safety

02:07:18.990 --> 02:07:20.730
are absolutely embedded within.

02:07:20.730 --> 02:07:25.140
So, I will continue to
work across the sector

02:07:25.140 --> 02:07:27.510
in those areas as well as
obviously within the remit

02:07:27.510 --> 02:07:29.940
of the Freedom to Speak Up Guardians.

02:07:29.940 --> 02:07:32.420
But my message to you
today is what more can you

02:07:32.420 --> 02:07:34.890
as NHS England leaders do?

02:07:34.890 --> 02:07:36.660
I'll be saying the same to CQC

02:07:36.660 --> 02:07:39.240
because seeing a continued deterioration

02:07:39.240 --> 02:07:41.610
in people's ability to
be psychologically safe

02:07:41.610 --> 02:07:44.850
to speak up about what matters
to them in the workplace,

02:07:44.850 --> 02:07:48.960
particularly patient safety
and worker safety is declining,

02:07:48.960 --> 02:07:51.890
and we can't see another
decline in another year.

02:07:51.890 --> 02:07:53.070
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

02:07:53.070 --> 02:07:53.903
- Andrew, do you want to comment

02:07:53.903 --> 02:07:56.550
because you do lead our interaction

02:07:56.550 --> 02:07:57.810
with the Guardians.

02:07:57.810 --> 02:08:01.290
- So I think, you know, the
really important bit for me

02:08:01.290 --> 02:08:03.750
is whether the local leadership,

02:08:03.750 --> 02:08:06.510
a local Board gets this or not?

02:08:06.510 --> 02:08:10.500
And it is down to the
chair and the chief exec.

02:08:10.500 --> 02:08:14.640
And in most organisations
it works well, right?

02:08:14.640 --> 02:08:18.300
And we've seen a different emphasis.

02:08:18.300 --> 02:08:22.770
We've seen lots of examples
where managers have listened

02:08:22.770 --> 02:08:25.500
or leaders have listened
and acted positively

02:08:25.500 --> 02:08:29.250
to concerns from staff.

02:08:29.250 --> 02:08:32.280
In some organisations
that is not the case.

02:08:32.280 --> 02:08:35.400
And I think we are just about to roll out

02:08:35.400 --> 02:08:37.320
the revised competencies

02:08:37.320 --> 02:08:39.900
for chairs, and chief exec, and NEDs.

02:08:39.900 --> 02:08:43.470
And one of the comments I
made was that we ought to put

02:08:43.470 --> 02:08:46.140
a couple of sentences in
there about the freedom

02:08:46.140 --> 02:08:48.480
to speak up kind of issues,

02:08:48.480 --> 02:08:49.710
and the leadership role

02:08:49.710 --> 02:08:52.290
that we're expecting them to discharge.

02:08:52.290 --> 02:08:54.003
'Cause I think it's really important

02:08:54.003 --> 02:08:57.427
that we make this as a kind
of mandatory element of,

02:08:57.427 --> 02:08:59.880
you know, good practise.

02:08:59.880 --> 02:09:02.286
And there is no excuse for this,

02:09:02.286 --> 02:09:03.780
you know, in my opinion.

02:09:03.780 --> 02:09:06.360
The Board's job is partly to listen

02:09:06.360 --> 02:09:08.490
to the feelings that staff,

02:09:08.490 --> 02:09:12.180
you know, want to make and
represent from time to time.

02:09:12.180 --> 02:09:15.780
So, I think we've made a
hell of a lot of progress,

02:09:15.780 --> 02:09:18.600
but we've got a hell of a lot more to do,

02:09:18.600 --> 02:09:21.480
particularly when the staff survey results

02:09:21.480 --> 02:09:23.269
show that we're going the wrong way.

02:09:23.269 --> 02:09:26.490
And I think you absolutely
right, Jane, to call that out.

02:09:26.490 --> 02:09:28.057
And we, along with the CQC, have got,

02:09:28.057 --> 02:09:30.390
you know, a big responsibility here.

02:09:30.390 --> 02:09:33.750
So if we can come
together, CQC can do this

02:09:33.750 --> 02:09:35.520
through the well-led element
- Yeah.

02:09:35.520 --> 02:09:37.320
- of their review and we do it

02:09:37.320 --> 02:09:41.070
through the practise
guidance that we issue,

02:09:41.070 --> 02:09:43.530
and set out the expectations

02:09:43.530 --> 02:09:46.350
that we have from boards that guardians

02:09:46.350 --> 02:09:49.827
have an open invitation to boards,

02:09:49.827 --> 02:09:52.590
the access to chief execs and chairs

02:09:52.590 --> 02:09:53.813
when things aren't going well.

02:09:53.813 --> 02:09:57.030
I mean, that's the ultimate route.

02:09:57.030 --> 02:09:59.460
But I think it's really important that we,

02:09:59.460 --> 02:10:00.527
you know, send the message out,

02:10:00.527 --> 02:10:04.320
and do this positively 'cause
it's a really important facet

02:10:04.320 --> 02:10:05.807
of, you know, good practise
- Yeah.

02:10:05.807 --> 02:10:07.530
- in the NHS.

02:10:07.530 --> 02:10:11.070
And the days of ignoring staff
are just completely gone.

02:10:11.070 --> 02:10:12.540
We cannot do that.

02:10:12.540 --> 02:10:15.540
They're too precious a
commodity to do that.

02:10:15.540 --> 02:10:19.170
And, you know, the organisations
that have difficulties

02:10:19.170 --> 02:10:21.480
over retention, if you actually look

02:10:21.480 --> 02:10:24.660
at their speak up activity,

02:10:24.660 --> 02:10:26.580
it's generally low.

02:10:26.580 --> 02:10:28.800
- Mm.
- It's generally low.

02:10:28.800 --> 02:10:32.490
So, you know, there's still
a lot to work on here,

02:10:32.490 --> 02:10:35.790
and I think together we can
make some further progress.

02:10:35.790 --> 02:10:37.024
- Yeah, thank you for saying that.

02:10:37.024 --> 02:10:39.930
- Thank you.
